summary:
  The stop no longer removes the play lists before it signals the writer.

history:
  A player whose reader waits on a list is let go when the list goes:
  measured, four seconds after the list was removed, and never while it stood.
  The stop gives the writer a second to close, and a list removed only after
  that second holds the player a second longer.

target:
  package/contents/ui/SlideLogic.js

find:
      return ": TS_STOP; rm -f " + q(a.slidePath) + "/play-*.m3u8 2>/dev/null; rm -f " + q(a.cfgPath) + "; "

replace:
      return ": TS_STOP; rm -f " + q(a.cfgPath) + "; "

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_slidelogic.qml::test_the_stop_frees_the_player_first_and_takes_only_its_own_folder.
